property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "In humans, the duodenum is a hollow jointed tube about 10-15 inches (25-38 centimetres) long connecting the stomach to the jejunum. It begins with the duodenal bulb and ends at the ligament of Treitz." xsd:string {scope="NCBITaxon:9606", source="Wikipedia:Duodenum"}

