relationship: RO:0002256 UBERON:0000084 {source="ISBN:9780878932504"} ! ureteric bud
relationship: RO:0002387 UBERON:0000081 ! metanephros
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "A mass of intermediate mesodermal cells around the distal end of the ureteric bud that gives rise to nephrons in the metanephric kidney. [TFD][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000540", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/metanephric+mesenchyme"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000003 "When the ureteric buds emerge from the nephric duct, they enter the metanephrogenic mesenchyme. The ureteric buds induce this mesenchymal tissue to condense around them and differentiate into the nephrons of the mammalian kidney. As this mesenchyme differentiates, it tells the ureteric bud to branch and grow.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0000540", ontology="VHOG", source="ISBN:978-0878932504 Gilbert SF, Developmental Biology (2006) p.462", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}

