property_value: foaf:depiction "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/Gray1109.png" xsd:anyURI
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "Either of the paired embryonic ducts developing into the uterine tubes, uterus, and vagina in the female and becoming largely obliterated in the male. [TFD][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001199", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/paramesonephric+duct"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "Transient developmental organ which gives rise to oviducts in female (documented to persist in some male frogs).[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0010141", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:RED"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000003 "In females, the archinephric (mesonephric) ducts tend to function only within the urinary systems. The muellerian duct arises embryologically next to the archinephric (wolffian) duct. In males, the muellerian duct regresses if it appears at all, but in females, the muellerian ducts become the oviducts of the reproductive system.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001199", ontology="VHOG", source="ISBN:978-0072528305 Kardong KV, Vertebrates: Comparative Anatomy, Function, Evolution (2006) p.559", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000011 "Sertoli cells secrete anti-Mullerian hormone (AMH) inducing the demise of this duct" xsd:string

