[Term]
id: UBERON:0005176
name: tooth enamel organ
def: "A circumscribed mass of ectodermal cells which bud off from the dental lamina; it becomes cup-shaped and develops on its internal face the ameloblast layer of cells that produces the enamel cap of a developing tooth." [https://github.com/cerivs/zebrafish-anatomical-ontology/issues/107, https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/1313, ISBN:0-683-40008-8, MP:0010747, Wikipedia:Enamel_organ]
comment: . Alternate definition: A cellular aggregation seen in histologic sections of a developing tooth. It lies above a condensation of ectomesenchymal cells called the odontogenic papilla.
subset: pheno_slim
subset: vertebrate_core
synonym: "dental organ" EXACT [ZFA:0005138]
synonym: "enamel organ" EXACT [MP:0010747]
synonym: "odontogenic organ" RELATED []
synonym: "organum enameleum" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Enamel_organ]
