[Term]
id: UBERON:0005313
name: mammary duct terminal end bud
def: "A unique club-shaped epithelial structure that develops at the tip of the mammary duct at the onset of puberty under the action of circulating hormones." [MGI:anna]
xref: EMAPA:37900 {source="MA:th"}
is_a: UBERON:0003244 ! epithelium of mammary gland
is_a: UBERON:0005153 ! epithelial bud
is_a: UBERON:0034969 ! epithelial layer of duct
relationship: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0001765 ! mammary duct
property_value: UBPROP:0000010 "terminal end buds (TEBs) consist of an outer layer of undifferentiated myoepithelial progenitor cells ('cap cells'), and a multilayered inner core of luminal epithelial cells ('body') fated to form the walls of the ductal lumen; both layers have high rates of mitosis, consistent with a motile organ dedicated to ductal morphogenesis" xsd:string
property_value: UBPROP:0000011 "TEBs proliferate, ramify, and actively invade the fad pad to allow the formation of a complex branching structure; this process of branching morphogenesis concludes at ~10-12 weeks of age in mice, when TEBs have traversed the length of the fat pad and a fully developed ductal tree has formed" xsd:string

