[Term]
id: UBERON:0005373
name: spinal cord dorsal column
def: "The wedge-shaped fiber bundle of white matter in the dorsomedial side of the spinal cord that is made up of the fasciculus gracilis and fasciculus cuneatus; it is part of the ascending posterior column-medial lemniscus pathway that is important for well-localized fine touch and conscious proprioception." [ISBN:0-683-40008-8, ISBN:0940780577, MP:0009677]
