xref: TAO:0001077
xref: ZFA:0001077
is_a: UBERON:0001048 ! primordium
is_a: UBERON:0003351 ! pharyngeal epithelium
relationship: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0000974 {gci_filler="NCBITaxon:40674", gci_relation="BFO:0000050", source="EHDAA2"} ! neck
relationship: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0002405 {source="ZFA"} ! immune system
relationship: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0003295 {source="EHDAA2"} ! pharyngeal gland
relationship: RO:0002254 UBERON:0005428 {notes="mesenchymal", source="ZFA", source="https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/wiki/The-neural-crest"} ! vagal neural crest
relationship: RO:0002254 UBERON:0010025 {gci_filler="NCBITaxon:8782", gci_relation="BFO:0000050", notes="Aves", source="ISBN:0073040584-table13.1"} ! dorsal part of pharyngeal pouch 3
relationship: RO:0002254 UBERON:0010026 {gci_filler="NCBITaxon:40674", gci_relation="BFO:0000050", notes="Mammals", source="EHDAA2", source="ISBN:0073040584-table13.1"} ! ventral part of pharyngeal pouch 3
relationship: RO:0002254 UBERON:0010027 {gci_filler="NCBITaxon:8782", gci_relation="BFO:0000050", notes="Aves", source="ISBN:0073040584-table13.1"} ! dorsal part of pharyngeal pouch 4
relationship: RO:0002254 UBERON:0010028 {gci_filler="NCBITaxon:40674", gci_relation="BFO:0000050", notes="Mammals", source="ISBN:0073040584-table13.1"} ! ventral part of pharyngeal pouch 4
property_value: IAO:0000116 "we follow Kardong table 13.1 in having some developmental contribution of pouch 4 in mammals, but this isn't reflected in EHDAA2. Consider adding distinct term for mesenchyme (see EHDAA2), to indicate NC constribution." xsd:string {source="ISBN:0781714125"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "A small outgrowth of the pharyngeal epithelium that is the site of lymphocyte cell production. Willett et al, 1999.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0001077", ontology="TAO", source="ZFIN:curator"}
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "variability of developmental origin: In fish, thymic primordia are generated by all the pouches except the first. However, in avians the thymus arises from pouches 3 and 4, whereas in humans it is only generated by the third pouch[PMID:16313389] The thymus arises from the second pouch in frogs, 2-6 in cartilaginous fish, 2-3 in reptiles, 3 or 4 in bony fish, birds and mammals. The final number is variable - 5 paired organs in sharks, 4 in caecilians, 3 in urodeles, 1 in many teleost, anurans and many mammals" xsd:string {source="ISBN:0781714125"}

