[Term]
id: UBERON:0006783
name: layer of superior colliculus
def: "The microstructure of the optic tectum / superior colliculus varies across species. As a general rule, there is always a clear distinction between superficial layers, which receive input primarily from the visual system and show primarily visual responses, and deeper layers, which receive many types of input and project to numerous motor-related brain areas. The distinction between these two zones is so clear and consistent that some anatomists have suggested that they should be considered separate brain structures. In mammals, neuroanatomists conventionally identify seven layers[WP]." [Wikipedia:Superior_colliculus#Neural_circuit]
synonym: "cytoarchitectural part of superior colliculus" EXACT [NLXANAT:1005033]
synonym: "layer of optic tectum" EXACT SENSU []
synonym: "tectal layer" RELATED SENSU []
xref: BAMS:SC-layers
xref: NLXANAT:1005033
xref: Wikipedia:Superior_colliculus#Neural_circuit
is_a: UBERON:0011215 ! central nervous system cell part cluster
is_a: UBERON:0022303 ! nervous system cell part layer
intersection_of: UBERON:0022303 ! nervous system cell part layer
intersection_of: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0001945 ! superior colliculus
relationship: BFO:0000050 UBERON:0001945 ! superior colliculus
property_value: UBPROP:0000008 "The tectum in lampreys has more layers than the tectum in hagfishes, likely related to the fact that vision is less well developed in hagfishes. tectal lamination is almost identical in reptiles and birds and is more restricted in mammals[http://icb.oxfordjournals.org/content/42/4/743.full]" xsd:string

